# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-1 windows (the ship-5 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt, ORDER-W2.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the three runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory and, since NP9, with the output
# ceiling of its catalog entry; the keys are the same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix, replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader
# refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint, which is what their question (exactness of reuse against a cold twin of the same boot; the platform sequence) does not depend on.
# A1 (EXACTNESS of the whole candidate, STOP): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s5-audit, the audited twin of the ship-5 candidate: every audit of the
# shipped ship-4 stack (the K/V page writer's audit of every unit it writes, the verify T2 audit, the pre-stage diff and two-block pre-stage audits, the multi-user SDPA
# launch's audit, the vglue, conv-gates and octo-lever audits, the 13x10 grids with all three sub-switches, the tile-aligned drafter window, the host tier with every
# instrument on, the host read-backs SAMPLED) plus what the candidate adds: the lone-user padded round (NP1), exact resume with its carry audit, the sliced restore at the
# 48 GiB tier and the 16 GiB checkpoint store, and the ONE lever the candidate does not carry, W3 WC (the GDN layer's windows, conv and gates in one launch, with its audit;
# F1's audit is out beside it), on Swift. Tests: warmup; coding (ONE user for 1,500 tokens: every round a lone-user padded round); np1_live2 (a pair: two idle segments,
# page 0 alone, the flag changes nothing); concurrent5_split (four users in block A and a fifth ALONE in block B, then a sixth: the split the placement leaves);
# concurrent8_drain (eight users whose budgets end one by one: every live count from 8 to 1, every split of the two blocks); concurrent8_steady (the octo rounds, required
# by the smoke check on this profile). Last, agent_turns on the audited twin. AGENT TURNS (agent_turns.py, tp4/agent-turns): SIX sessions of 64k, 128k and 200k tokens of
# coding context, each a cold opening request and then 12 returning turns (a ~150-400 token tool result appended after the previous answer verbatim, 200-600 tokens out, a
# 1-8 s tool gap), every session under its own cache_salt (the smoke step writes a throwaway salt key and mounts it only for this test). It is the one smoke that reaches
# the prefix store, sticky sessions, the engine rebind, exact resume (the undrop and the carry) and the lone-user round at the live counts a real conversation mix produces.
# A MEASUREMENT, no speed threshold: the judge fails an errored or timed-out request, a request with no tokens or no finish, and a salted run that reuses nothing on more
# than 10% of its returning turns. The six contexts total about 800,000 tokens of the 1,055,488-token pool, so it does not force the host tier (A3 does). `python3
# scripts/ci/agent_turns.py report --smoke-log <smoke> --container-log <container>` prints the rates, the TTFT by context bucket, the re-prefilled tokens and the per-live
# table; run it on both legs of the pair and set them side by side. READ: c2_smoke_check clean (its fusion, octo, grid13 and WC rules read the container log); every audit
# line exact=True with entries above 0; octo_judge.py --container-log <container log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s5-audit clean; the NP1
# lines in the container log: "[NP1] kv scratch: Qwen36ForCausalLM.allocate_kv_cache allocates 1 block(s) beyond the pool vLLM sized (pool 16500 blocks, scratch ids
# 16500..16500)" once, "[SOLO-PACKED] admitted min_users=1 scratch_pages=16500 (gate only)" once and, for each of the two M3 blocks, "packed padded block admitted
# min_users=1 users=4 max_idle=4 ... scratch_pages=16500"; the octo block's own admitted line is unchanged (min_users=6, max_idle=2, no scratch pages); NO "audit mismatch",
# NO "fell back" (the WC rule alone accepts the one "fell back reason=8 users" line, the octo block: WC takes 2 or 4 users), NO "kv shared", NO "page0 ... refused" for an
# eligible lone user, no stall. The memory ledger's free DRAM per chip after the attach: RECORD it. THE FIRST COMPILE OF THE WC KERNELS IS THIS JOB (they have never been
# through a compiler): when the log shows the attach stopping at a WC compile error or a "gdn wc" refusal and at nothing else, that is a fault of an UNSHIPPED lever, not of
# the candidate: run A1N (the same job on the twin without WC) and keep the window going; ANY other failure is NO-GO for the candidate and halts the window. CHECKPOINT READ
# (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models
# answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through
# the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the
# lever. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. Duration (estimate): 110
# minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s5-audit
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,np1_live2,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=180
